                <pb facs="0279" n="268" sameAs="frus:frus1937v02/pg268"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">611.60131/63: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Estonia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Leonard</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tallinn</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-04-28T17:00:00+02:00">April 28, 1937—5
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received April 30—6:40 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>6. With reference to the Department’s telegram No. 4, April 26, 6 p.m. relative
                    to the extension of the Treaty of Commerce. Note <pb facs="0280" n="269"
                        xml:id="pg269"/> suggested by the Department delivered today and will be
                    given consideration by the Foreign Office after Mr. Wirgo returns shortly from
                    Finland.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Leonard</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
